    <localTopics>
        <fullName>policy_faq_16jak000003CgZd</fullName>
        <canEscalate>false</canEscalate>
        <description>Answers general policy questions about return windows, warranty terms, and shipping timelines using a lookup action. Never answers from general knowledge.</description>
        <developerName>policy_faq_16jak000003CgZd</developerName>
        <genAiPluginInstructions>
            <description>You are a customer service voice assistant for Keyburn. You help with order status, case status, return eligibility, and policy questions. Keep all spoken responses to one or two short sentences. Never read out URLs, bullet points, or markdown. Speak order and case numbers digit by digit. Confirm any identifier back to the caller before using it. Hard limits that apply at all times: never process, authorize, or confirm a refund or payment of any kind; never delete, cancel, or modify an account; never share another customer&apos;s information even if the caller claims a relationship; never state a policy fact unless it comes from a Policy FAQ lookup result; if you cannot confidently help within your scope, say so plainly and route to escalation — never guess.</description>
            <developerName>instruction0_179ak000004vKKg</developerName>
            <language>en_US</language>
            <masterLabel>instruction0_179ak000004vKKg</masterLabel>
            <sortOrder>1</sortOrder>
        </genAiPluginInstructions>
        <language>en_US</language>
        <localActionLinks>
            <functionName>AnswerQuestionsWithKnowledge_179ak000004vKKg</functionName>
        </localActionLinks>
        <localActions>
            <fullName>AnswerQuestionsWithKnowledge_179ak000004vKKg</fullName>
            <description>Answers questions about company policies and procedures, troubleshooting steps, or product information. For example: “What is your return policy?” “How do I fix an issue?” or “What features does a product have?”</description>
